+# Galaxy S23 Ultra SM-S9180 / S9180ZHS8FZF5 port record
+
+This record contains the exact inputs and derived values for the Snapdragon 8 Gen 2 (Kalama) Galaxy S23 Ultra profile `dm3q-S9180ZHS8FZF5`. The kernel features Samsung's KDP (Kernel Data Protection), RKP, and DEFEX hardening, requiring specialized offset derivation and KernelSU patching.
+
+## Firmware identity and acquisition
+
+Samsung FUS was queried for model `SM-S9180`, region `BRI`
+The extracted firmware properties are:
+
+```text
+model: SM-S9180
+device: dm3q
+display build: BP4A.251205.006.S9180ZHS8FZF5
+fingerprint: samsung/dm3qzhx/dm3q:16/BP4A.251205.006/S9180ZHS8FZF5:user/release-keys
+SDK: 36
+ABI: arm64-v8a
+kernel release: 5.15.189-android13-8-33413713-abS9180ZHS8FZF5
+kernel build: #1 SMP PREEMPT Mon Jun 15 08:10:25 UTC 2026
+```
+
+## Symbol and BTF recovery
+
+`vmlinux-to-elf` recovered symbols at image base `0xffffffc008000000`. Required offsets below came from manual reverse engineering and cross-referencing the recovered S9180 ELF.
+
+Crucially, `TASK_STRUCT_CRED_OFF` was conclusively verified at `0x5e0` by tracing the KDP (Kernel Data Protection) validation checks and `task_group` overwrite vectors inside `rt_mutex_lock` and `process_one_work`.
+
+| Macro/use | Symbol or derivation | Offset |
+| --- | --- | ---: |
+| `TASK_STRUCT_CRED_OFF` | `cred` inside `task_struct` (verified via KDP check) | `0x5e0` |
+| `TASK_STRUCT_REAL_CRED_OFF` | `real_cred` inside `task_struct` | `0x5d8` |
+| `INIT_TASK_OFF` | `init_task` | `0x02c05080` |
+| `SELINUX_ENFORCING_OFF` | `selinux_state.enforcing` | `0x02a3c404` |
+| `KMALLOC_CACHES_OFF` | `kmalloc_caches` | `0x020641f8` |
+| `ANON_PIPE_BUF_OPS_OFF` | `anon_pipe_buf_ops` | `0x01e7f1e0` |
+| `SYSTEM_UNBOUND_WQ_OFF` | `system_unbound_wq` | `0x02a90800` |
+| `CALL_USERMODEHELPER_EXEC_WORK_OFF` | `call_usermodehelper_exec_work` | `0x001045d0` |
+| `ROOT_TASK_GROUP_OFF` | `root_task_group` | `0x02cb9ac0` |
+| `ASHMEM_FOPS_OFF` | `ashmem_fops` | `0x0200d238` |
+| `CONFIGFS_READ_ITER_OFF` | `configfs_read_iter` | `0x005d7420` |
+| `COPY_SPLICE_READ_OFF` | `copy_splice_read` | `0x00528198` |
